{"title":"Career roadmap — Research Associate (Political Science)","role":"Research Associate (Political Science)","summary":"A Research Associate in Political Science supports academic, policy, governance, political-risk, public-affairs, think-tank, and social-impact research. The role involves literature reviews, data collection, policy analysis, interviews, survey research, qualitative/quantitative analysis, report writing, and evidence-based recommendations.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Political Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build political science foundations, research methodology, statistics, academic writing, policy research, internships and research projects"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in public policy, international relations, governance, political economy, elections, development or comparative politics"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move into Senior Research Associate, Research Fellow, Policy Analyst, Project Lead or specialised political-risk roles"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead research programmes, think-tank portfolios, policy initiatives, consulting practices or academic research teams"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Political science foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political theory"},{"text":"Indian political system"},{"text":"Constitution and institutions"},{"text":"Comparative politics"},{"text":"Political thinkers"},{"text":"Public administration basics"},{"text":"Introduction to sociology and economics"},{"text":"Academic reading and note-making"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Research ethics"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Output","text":"Write 3–5 short research papers on political or governance issues."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Research methodology"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Interview methodology"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Citation and referencing"},{"text":"SPSS/R/Python basics"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Policy brief writing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government datasets"},{"text":"Election data"},{"text":"Census and socioeconomic data"},{"text":"Parliamentary/public documents"},{"text":"International datasets"},{"text":"Academic journals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one or two areas:"},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Useful subjects"],"rows":[[{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Policy analysis, governance, programme evaluation"}],[{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"Geopolitics, diplomacy, security studies"}],[{"text":"Political Economy"},{"text":"Economics, development, institutions"}],[{"text":"Indian Politics"},{"text":"Elections, parties, federalism, public institutions"}],[{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Public administration, decentralisation, service delivery"}],[{"text":"Conflict & Security"},{"text":"Conflict studies, terrorism studies, strategic affairs"}],[{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"Poverty, education, health, gender, livelihoods"}],[{"text":"Election Research"},{"text":"Electoral behaviour, polling, campaign analytics"}],[{"text":"Political Communication"},{"text":"Media, public opinion, political communication"}],[{"text":"Environmental Politics"},{"text":"Climate policy, environmental governance, sustainability"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-year projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong projects could include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"State-level comparison of public-service delivery"},{"text":"Analysis of voting behaviour using election datasets"},{"text":"Impact evaluation of a government welfare programme"},{"text":"Comparative study of electoral systems"},{"text":"Political representation and gender"},{"text":"Social media and political communication"},{"text":"Centre–state relations in India"},{"text":"AI and the future of democratic governance"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["The project should ideally produce a research paper","dataset","visualisations","policy brief."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Skills to develop","Potential roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Policy analysis, programme evaluation"},{"text":"Policy Researcher"}],[{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Institutions, administration, public programmes"},{"text":"Governance Analyst"}],[{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"Geopolitics, diplomacy, security"},{"text":"IR Researcher"}],[{"text":"Political Economy"},{"text":"Economics + politics"},{"text":"Political Economy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Elections"},{"text":"Survey research, electoral data"},{"text":"Election Researcher"}],[{"text":"Development"},{"text":"Impact evaluation, development economics"},{"text":"Development Research Associate"}],[{"text":"Security"},{"text":"Conflict analysis, strategic studies"},{"text":"Security Researcher"}],[{"text":"Political Communication"},{"text":"Media, public opinion, digital analytics"},{"text":"Political Communication Analyst"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Particularly valuable technical stack"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","R/Python","SQL basics","Power BI/Tableau","GIS","research databases","AI-assisted research"]},{"type":"p","text":"For a modern political-science researcher, combining social-science reasoning + data analysis is considerably stronger than relying only on theoretical knowledge."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"Public-policy organisations"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Research centres"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Government-policy projects"},{"text":"International development organisations"},{"text":"Political research organisations"},{"text":"Election research organisations"},{"text":"Public-affairs firms"},{"text":"Governance consulting firms"},{"text":"Media research desks"},{"text":"Legislative research organisations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Policy Research Intern"},{"text":"Public Policy Intern"},{"text":"Governance Research Intern"},{"text":"Political Research Intern"},{"text":"Legislative Research Intern"},{"text":"Data Research Intern"},{"text":"International Relations Research Intern"},{"text":"Development Research Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What to produce during internships"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not focus only on receiving a certificate."},{"type":"p","text":"Try to produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature reviews"},{"text":"Research notes"},{"text":"Policy briefs"},{"text":"Survey datasets"},{"text":"Interview transcripts"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Research reports"},{"text":"Infographics"},{"text":"Background papers"},{"text":"Presentation decks"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications and learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Useful learning"],"rows":[[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Research Methodology"}],[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Statistics for Social Sciences"}],[{"text":"Data"},{"text":"Excel, R, Python"}],[{"text":"Policy"},{"text":"Public Policy Analysis"}],[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"QGIS / ArcGIS fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Survey research"},{"text":"Survey Design & Sampling"}],[{"text":"Writing"},{"text":"Academic & Policy Writing"}],[{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"IR / Security Studies"}],[{"text":"Development"},{"text":"Development Economics / Impact Evaluation"}],[{"text":"Digital research"},{"text":"OSINT & information verification"}],[{"text":"AI"},{"text":"AI-assisted research & data analysis"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, research outputs and methodological competence generally matter more than collecting many certificates."}]},{"heading":"Careers you can be hired as","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Direct roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Associate"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Political Research Associate"},{"text":"Policy Research Associate"},{"text":"Public Policy Researcher"},{"text":"Governance Researcher"},{"text":"Political Analyst"},{"text":"Research Analyst"},{"text":"Programme Research Associate"},{"text":"Legislative Research Associate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Adjacent roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy Analyst"},{"text":"Public Affairs Analyst"},{"text":"Government Affairs Analyst"},{"text":"Political Risk Analyst"},{"text":"Development Analyst"},{"text":"Monitoring & Evaluation Analyst"},{"text":"Social Researcher"},{"text":"International Relations Analyst"},{"text":"Programme Analyst"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Long-term roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Research Fellow"},{"text":"Policy Advisor"},{"text":"Research Director"},{"text":"Programme Director"},{"text":"Think-Tank Director"},{"text":"Public Policy Consultant"},{"text":"Political Risk Consultant"},{"text":"Professor / Academic Researcher"},{"text":"Governance Specialist"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For serious research careers, a postgraduate degree is strongly recommended."},{"type":"table","header":["PG route","Best for"],"rows":[[{"text":"MA Political Science"},{"text":"Political theory, Indian politics, comparative politics"}],[{"text":"MA Public Policy"},{"text":"Policy and governance"}],[{"text":"MA International Relations"},{"text":"Diplomacy and geopolitics"}],[{"text":"MA Development Studies"},{"text":"Development and social policy"}],[{"text":"MA Governance/Public Administration"},{"text":"Government and administration"}],[{"text":"MA Political Economy"},{"text":"Economics + political analysis"}],[{"text":"MA/MSc Data & Social Research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"}],[{"text":"Master of Public Policy (MPP)"},{"text":"Applied policy careers"}],[{"text":"PhD Political Science"},{"text":"Academic/advanced research"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended route"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science","Research Internships","MA/Master's in Political Science/Public Policy/IR","Research Associate","Senior Researcher/Policy Analyst","Research Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"For a highly quantitative policy career:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science","MA/MSc Data/Policy Research","Research/Data Analyst","Policy Research Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Study abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Strong areas"],"rows":[[{"text":"🇬🇧 UK"},{"text":"Political Science, Public Policy, IR, Development"}],[{"text":"🇺🇸 USA"},{"text":"Political Science, Public Policy, Political Economy"}],[{"text":"🇨🇦 Canada"},{"text":"Public Policy, Governance, Political Science"}],[{"text":"🇦🇺 Australia"},{"text":"Public Policy, Development, International Relations"}],[{"text":"🇩🇪 Germany"},{"text":"Political Science, European Studies, Public Policy"}],[{"text":"🇳🇱 Netherlands"},{"text":"Governance, European Politics, International Relations"}],[{"text":"🇸🇬 Singapore"},{"text":"Asian politics, public policy, international affairs"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful master's areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political Science"},{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"Public Administration"},{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"Political Economy"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Security Studies"},{"text":"Quantitative Social Science"},{"text":"Data Science for Social Sciences"}]}]},{"heading":"Career progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Intern","Research Assistant","Research Associate","Senior Research Associate","Research Fellow / Policy Analyst","Senior Research Fellow","Research Lead / Programme Director","Research Director / Think-Tank Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Policy pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Associate","Policy Analyst","Senior Policy Analyst","Policy Advisor","Policy Lead","Policy Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Associate","Social Data Analyst","Quantitative Researcher","Senior Data/Policy Analyst","Research Lead"]},{"type":"note","label":"Emerging specialisations","text":"2030–2040"},{"type":"p","text":"Political research is likely to become increasingly interdisciplinary."},{"type":"h","text":"1. AI & Democracy"},{"type":"p","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-generated political content"},{"text":"Deepfakes"},{"text":"Algorithmic political influence"},{"text":"AI regulation"},{"text":"Digital democracy"},{"text":"Election integrity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Computational Political Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine political science with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"NLP"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Network analysis"},{"text":"Sentiment analysis"},{"text":"Social-media datasets"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Political Risk Intelligence"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Elections"},{"text":"Government changes"},{"text":"Geopolitical instability"},{"text":"Regulatory changes"},{"text":"Conflict"},{"text":"Trade policy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Climate & Political Economy"},{"type":"p","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Climate policy"},{"text":"Energy transitions"},{"text":"Carbon markets"},{"text":"Resource politics"},{"text":"Climate migration"},{"text":"Environmental governance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Evidence-Based Governance"},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data","Research","Evaluation","Policy recommendation","Impact measurement"]},{"type":"p","text":"This will be valuable across governments, think tanks, international organisations and consulting."},{"type":"note","label":"2040–2046","text":"How the role evolves"},{"type":"p","text":"The traditional Research Associate role will increasingly become an AI-augmented research position."},{"type":"p","text":"AI will assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature discovery"},{"text":"Document classification"},{"text":"Dataset preparation"},{"text":"Transcription"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Text analysis"},{"text":"Policy-document comparison"},{"text":"Visualisation"},{"text":"Research monitoring"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But researchers will remain responsible for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Source verification"},{"text":"Methodological validity"},{"text":"Causal reasoning"},{"text":"Interpretation"},{"text":"Ethical judgement"},{"text":"Bias detection"},{"text":"Policy implications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The highest-value researchers will therefore combine domain expertise + methodology + data + critical thinking."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Political Science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political theory"},{"text":"Indian politics"},{"text":"Comparative politics"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Political economy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Qualitative methods"},{"text":"Quantitative methods"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Case-study methodology"},{"text":"Academic writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"R/Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI/Tableau"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Modern research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OSINT"},{"text":"Digital research"},{"text":"NLP"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"},{"text":"Fact-checking"},{"text":"Source verification"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy writing"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Stakeholder interviews"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Research ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Political science + research fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Research methodology + statistics + internships"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Specialisation + data research + major project"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Research Assistant / Research Associate"}],[{"text":"Years 1–3"},{"text":"Build research portfolio + PG preparation"}],[{"text":"Years 3–6"},{"text":"MA/MPP + Research Associate/Policy Analyst"}],[{"text":"Years 6–10"},{"text":"Senior Researcher / Policy Analyst / Research Fellow"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Research Lead / Policy Advisor / Research Director"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Science","strong research methodology","statistics","Excel/R/Python","policy writing","internships","MA/MPP","published research/policy briefs"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Key principle","text":"A strong Political Science Research Associate should not be limited to reading and writing. The strongest profile combines political theory, rigorous research methodology, data analysis, source verification, policy understanding and clear evidence-based communication."}]}]}